      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: We should assert that the new `target` being discarded does not contain Starlark metadata. If it does, we are silently dropping it (which could happen if a Starlark target was accessed via `to_rust` prior to its registration, or if it is accidentally registered twice).\n\n```rust\n            Entry::Occupied(e) \u003d\u003e {\n                assert!(\n                    target.starlark.is_none(),\n                    \"Target already registered, or accessed via to_rust before registration\"\n                );\n                // Safety: A target object in the map is never deleted and lives for the\n                // session.\n                unsafe { extend_lifetime(\u0026**e.get()) }\n            },\n```",
